\section{Sturm--Liouville Reduction and KK Mode Structure}

In this section we derive the full Sturm--Liouville eigenvalue problem governing
the Kaluza--Klein (KK) tower in the STME-RS-A framework. The presence of the
anharmonic bulk potential modifies both the eigenfunctions and eigenvalues,
leading to non-equidistant KK masses. We present analytic approximations,
numerical solutions, and figure-based comparisons between harmonic and
anharmonic regimes.

\subsection{Eigenvalue Problem}

We expand the bulk scalar field $\Phi(x,y)$ in KK modes:
\begin{equation}
\Phi(x,y) = \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \phi_n(x) f_n(y),
\end{equation}
where $f_n(y)$ are eigenfunctions of the Sturm--Liouville operator
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{L}[f_n] = -\frac{1}{e^{-4k|y|}} \frac{d}{dy}
\left( e^{-4k|y|} \frac{df_n}{dy} \right)
+ \frac{d^2 V}{d\Phi^2} f_n.
\end{equation}

The eigenvalue equation is
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{L}[f_n] = m_n^2 f_n,
\label{eq:SL}
\end{equation}
with orthonormality condition
\begin{equation}
\int_0^L dy\, e^{-2k|y|} f_n(y) f_m(y) = \delta_{nm}.
\end{equation}

