\subsection{Analytic Approximations}

To first order in $\lambda_4$, the mass shift is
\begin{equation}
\Delta m_n^2 \approx
\frac{12\lambda_4}{16\lambda^2}
\left( 6n^2 + 6n + 3 \right).
\label{eq:mass_shift}
\end{equation}

Thus the full mass spectrum is
\begin{equation}
m_n^2 =
4k^2
+ 2\sqrt{\lambda}\left(n+\tfrac{1}{2}\right)
+ \Delta m_n^2.
\end{equation}

The deviation from equidistance is quantified by
\begin{equation}
\delta_{12} = \frac{m_2}{m_1} - 2, \qquad
\delta_{23} = \frac{m_3}{m_2} - \frac{m_2}{m_1}.
\end{equation}

