\subsection{Numerical Solutions}

We solve Eq.~(\ref{eq:SL}) numerically using a finite-difference discretization
with IR-localized boundary conditions. The eigenfunctions exhibit increased
localization near the IR brane as $\lambda_4$ increases.

\begin{figure}[h!]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.75\textwidth]{fig_KK_wavefunctions.pdf}
\caption{KK wavefunctions $f_n(y)$ for $n=1,2,3$ in harmonic and anharmonic
cases. Anharmonicity increases IR localization and shifts eigenvalues upward.}
\label{fig:KK_wavefunctions}
\end{figure}

The numerical eigenvalues match the analytic approximation in
Eq.~(\ref{eq:mass_shift}) to within 3\% for the benchmark points BP1--BP4.

